//     Discord keeps short hashes (1900-char budget).
//  C2 email has (almost) no truncation: wordCut/trim ONLY for Discord paths
//     (notification_text + discord_embed); email_html shows full AI summary,
//     full AI technique reasons, timeline up to 15, related up to 15, all TI
//     rows full, observables full; ellipsis only as absolute safety-net (>2000 chars).
//  N1 embed Rule value has no "Rule" prefix (field name already Rule).
//  N2 email metric middle box keeps descriptive value, small label removed.
//  N3 empty cells render em-dash.
//  N4 VirusTotal renders "flagged by N engines" (never x/y without denominator).
//  N5 Discord TI headline picks hottest indicator (max VT malicious) as
//     "[Type] value — Verdict (detail)"; primary IP still in Evidence.
//
// Differences vs v2 (all content defects fixed, Discord EMBED added):
//  B2 AI summary cuts at word boundary; confidence is its own clause.
//  B3 every playbook returns exactly 4 steps (Actions always numbered 1-4).
//  B4 auth-only "Login success" line; Why prefers strong reasons over public-IP filler.
//  B5 MITRE rule shows technique NAMES via MITRE_NAMES map (local_rules.xml + standard).
//  B6 email cells truncate at word boundary + ellipsis. B7 unknown sources => Unknown.
//  B8 metrics read "4 IPs / 3 users". B9 hashes shown middle-shortened.
//  B10 timeline marker is its own Flag column. B11 report button verified.
//  A3 new output field discord_embed ({username, embeds[]} ready to POST to a webhook).
//
// Differences vs v1:
//  - notification_text is PLAIN TEXT (no emoji, no markdown) for Discord, max 1900 chars.
//  - Adds email_subject ([LEVEL] verdict — incident) + email_html (Sentinel-style,
//    inline CSS only, no external dependencies).
//  - Empty fields are OMITTED (never rendered as "none"/"-").
//  - Actions are always a numbered 1-4 deterministic playbook per attack_type.
//  - Smart truncate protects header + Why + Full report link + analyst note.

